Subject: [PATCH 3/3] docs(install): explain duplicate protobuf descriptor
 registration error

Co-authored-by: justinchuby <11205048+justinchuby@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 INSTALL.md | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/INSTALL.md b/INSTALL.md
index fa71def3d8d..1ede2338c42 100644
--- a/INSTALL.md
+++ b/INSTALL.md
@@ -259,3 +259,5 @@ For full list refer to CMakeLists.txt
 * If you run into any issues while building Protobuf as a static library, please ensure that shared Protobuf libraries, like libprotobuf, are not installed on your device or in the conda environment. If these shared libraries exist, either remove them to build Protobuf from source as a static library, or skip the Protobuf build from source to use the shared version directly.
 
 * If you run into any issues while building ONNX from source, and your error message reads, `Could not find pythonXX.lib`, ensure that you have consistent Python versions for common commands, such as `python` and `pip`. Clean all existing build files and rebuild ONNX again.
+
+* If a process aborts with `File already exists in database: onnx/onnx-ml.proto`, it holds more than one copy of the generated ONNX protobuf objects while sharing a single Protobuf runtime, and the second copy fails to register its descriptors. This typically happens when several components that each statically link ONNX (for example two Python extension modules) are loaded together. Make sure every component in the process uses the same single copy of ONNX, for example by building ONNX with `BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON` and linking `ONNX::onnx` (which pulls in `ONNX::onnx_proto`) against that shared library.
